   "source": [
    "# Measuring distance : Now we will follow euclidean distance to find the shortest distance between 2 points."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Reference : https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_distance , https://flexiple.com/python/calculate-distance-python"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#Function for calculating euclidean distance\n",
    "def euclidean_distance(city1: Tuple[float, float], city2: Tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n",
    "    return np.sqrt((city1[0] - city2[0])**2 + (city1[1] - city2[1])**2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "50.17136010935256\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#Sample distance calculation between 2 cities\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "This is a sample how the line of code is calculating distance . \n",
    "From the sample_cities variable we are taking the iloc and the X and Y coordinate values. After that passing this in the euclidean \n",
    "distance function which is calculating the distance between 2 points\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "print(euclidean_distance((sample_cities.iloc[0]['X'], sample_cities.iloc[0]['Y']), (sample_cities.iloc[1]['X'], sample_cities.iloc[1]['Y'])))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we will create a function which will calculate total distance from a list"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Here this function does a total tour and calculates the net covered distance\n",
    "# Each time the loop is running it is adding distance covered and upto returning\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "This function is calculating total distance covered. Here we are passing a list of the available paths and then it is going in \n",
    "a loop which is adding distance between 2 cities and then doing a sum\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "def calculate_total_distance(tour: List[int], cities: np.ndarray) -> float:\n",
    "    total_dist = 0.0\n",
    "    for i in range(len(tour)):\n",
    "        city1 = cities[tour[i]]\n",
    "        city2 = cities[tour[(i + 1) % len(tour)]]\n",
    "        total_dist += euclidean_distance(city1, city2)\n",
    "    return total_dist"
   ]
  },
